                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's old and has a little jank. If you're familiar with 90s/00s-era pc games, this will feel familiar. If you can get past those boundaries, this is one of the best-written worlds I've ever experienced. The depth of the ethical questions contained in this world is impressive, even if it takes itself \"too seriously\" sometimes. The lore is cool to get sucked into. The game mechanics, for a turn-based rpg, are plenty fun. Spells, summoning, combat, but also mechanics, diplomacy, clever tricks. The biggest appeal is that instead of recruiting NPCs in the world to join your party, you create mutant monsters, a mechanic which is imbedded at the heart of the sci-fi fantasy drama this game holds. \r\n\r\nThere's a large degree of freedom in this game. 3 classes to choose from and 4 optional factions you can join. You could slaughter every single living creature in this game and still complete it. You could also not hurt a fly. I have mounds of nostalgia for this series. If this sounds appealing, but you can't get past the noticeable age of the graphics and UI, check out the 2025 remake, Geneforge 2 - Infestation. It's got even more content and many quality-of-life fixes.",
